# SvelteKit Project Structure

## File & Folder Conventions

- Routes in `src/routes` (SvelteKit file-based routing); shared code in `src/lib`.
- Components: `src/lib/components/ComponentName/ComponentName.svelte` with an `index.ts` barrel export.
- Utilities: `src/lib/utils`; shared types: `src/lib/types`.
- PascalCase for component files/folders, camelCase for utilities, kebab-case for route files.
- If the project uses route groups (e.g. `(panel)`), put new pages inside the existing group unless told otherwise.

## UI Kit Policy

- If the project has a UI kit dependency, ALWAYS check it for an existing component (Button, Input, Card, Table, ...) before writing custom markup. Import from the package — never copy kit source into the repo.
- Compose kit components via props/snippets. Build a custom component only when the kit has no match.
- If the kit exposes a component catalog/doc source, consult it instead of guessing prop names.
